the 70th annual Primetime Emmy Awards  were held September 17th 2018 in Los  Angeles and like all award ceremonies  they were a wild mix of good and bad  depending on where you were and who you  were rooting for relive the night with  our picks for the 5 best and 5 worst  moments from the show best Henry Winkler  strikes gold Henry Winkler known best as  Fonzie from Happy Days seems to be a  genuinely nice guy who deserves all his  success so it was great to see Winkler's  talents shine again in a big way on the  HBO hit berry and it was even better to  see him finally take home an Emmy Award  for acting after five previous  nominations  according to Winkler he wrote his  acceptance speech when he was first  nominated in 1976 which became  hilariously obvious when he gave a  shout-out to his now adult children Jed  Zoe and max you could go to bed now  daddy won worst banter isn't always  better  this year's Emmys opened with a  tongue-in-cheek song about how Hollywood  has finally solved its diversity problem  complete with the hilarious talents of a  diverse set of stars  [Music]  the funny statement-making opening  showed promise for an exciting evening  that is until host Colin Jost and  Michael che took the stage the goofy  musical act proved to be a hard act to  follow for the SNL Weekend Update hosts  who seemed a little too stiff  perhaps the hosts fell out of place when  plucked from behind the news desk or  maybe their joke seemed a bit too eager  to get a rise out of the audience  whatever the case this was an opening  that just never quite landed that's  incredible best  all hail Betty White one of the most  joyous moments of the night happened  when Kate McKinnon and Alec Baldwin took  the stage to introduce a woman who needs  no introduction Betty White the audience  went wild when white appeared giving her  a lengthy standing ovation as she gave  brief remarks cracked a couple of jokes  and seemed genuinely in awe of the  welcome she was met with no awards were  given but it was nice to have a moment  of well-deserved recognition for  everyone's favorite golden girl  [Applause]  [Music]  worst the Emmy history bits to further  emphasize the seven decades of Emmys  history a and just called up Fred  Armisen and Maya Rudolph to act as Emmy  history correspondents throughout the  show this had the potential to be an  extremely funny recurring bit  considering the gag was that Armisen and  Rudolph apparently didn't do any  research for the gig you guys know  everything there is to know about the  Emmys okay unfortunately the comedic  talents of these to SNL veterans were  wasted on seemingly pointless bits that  were made even more awkward by che and  Jos lack of enthusiasm once again out of  time best Teddy Perkins's appearance  fans of Donald Glover's Atlanta were  delighted during the Emmys broadcast  when Teddy Perkins was spotted in the  star-studded audience even hugging Emmy  winner Bill Hader Perkins an eccentric  character from the Atlanta episode aptly  titled Teddy Perkins quickly made a name  for himself after appearing in just one  episode this was due partly to Perkins  is sheer strangeness and partly to the  mystery of who exactly was playing him  seeing Perkins pop up again at the Emmys  was so unexpected that the moment was  instantly one of the night's big winners  worst the weird presentation format if  the 2018 Emmys format seemed a little  different than usual  that's because it was instead of having  presenters come out and banter for a  moment before presenting the nominees  and reading the winners name the 2018  nominees names came first followed by  the introduction of the presenters who  then bantered and read the winners name  it was a nice effort to break up the  expected order of things but it didn't  really work yeah best the live marriage  proposal director Glenn Weiss made sure  we'd never forget his 2018 Emmys moment  when he accepted the outstanding  directing for a variety special Emmy for  his work directing the 2018 Oscars Weiss  began his remarks by memorializing his  mother who passed away just two weeks  prior before shifting his focus to his  girlfriend Jan who is sitting in the  audience you wonder why I don't like to  call you my girlfriend because I want to  call you my wife to add an extra layer  of heartwarming joy to the surprise  proposal Weiss revealed that he'd gotten  permission from his father to use the  same ring his late mother had worn talk  about stealing the show Worst the  reparation Emmys sometimes good ideas  simply don't live up to their full  potential  case in point Michael J's reparation  Emmy segment in the pre-taped bit che  attempted to highlight the lack of  diversity in previous Emmy ceremonies by  presenting trophies to various black TV  stars unfortunately it all seemed  undercut by Jays apparent determination  to act like he didn't need to be there  add a nil time to Bill Cosby reference  and you have the recipe for a truly  lackluster segment spite its potential  to be both statement-making and  hilarious let's just say I stole it from  Bill Cosby best hannah gatsby steals the  show  Hannah Gatsby's Nanette was 20 18 s most  talked-about comedy special so it wasn't  exactly surprising when she walked out  on the Emmy stage to hand out the award  for outstanding directing in a Drama  Series unsurprisingly Gadsby sidestepped  the usual teleprompter driven speech and  delivered effortlessly funny jokes  poking fun at the response to her  special you know hash tag no Roman but a  lot of them the whole thing was  perfectly capped off when Stephen Daldry  won the award for his work on the crown  but wasn't in attendance leaving Gadsby  to accept on his behalf so I think I  just leave now and that's worst the  Americans brush with glory throughout  six seasons on FX spy drama the  Americans was a show that both critics  and devoted fans loved but it seemed  like the emmy simply never got it  however it's four nominations at the  2018 Emmys suggested a possible final  chance at glory for one of the best  shows of its era we had a job to do when  the show won for both outstanding  writing and outstanding actor fans of  the Americans were hopeful that Keri  Russell would win an Emmy for her  impressive work on the show however  Russell lost out to the equally  deserving Claire Foy the show's  outstanding drama lost a game of Thrones  was the final gut punch to fans and  critics who have rooted for the show for  years and proved that sometimes  popularity wins over substance  [Music]
 

